    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        40,
        -560
      ],
      "size": [
        720,
        620
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 50,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## How to make videos\n\n1. In the **bigLust** recipe (other tab), click your picture(s), then\n   **Send to Video Queue**.\n2. Here: click a slot, type the MOTION in the right prompt box (what should\n   move), pick a size / length, press **Run**.\n3. Each clip **auto-saves** to `output/freedom_video/`. STEP 9 also has\n   **Set User Save Folder** / **Save to my folder**, and **Extend video\n   length** (joins more onto the end).\n\n## This is the 14-billion model - slower, better\nTwo \"experts\" run in sequence per clip: STEP 7a lays down the big motion,\nSTEP 7b polishes detail. On a 12 GB card a 5-second clip is roughly\n**8-15 minutes**. The 10/15/20 s presets chain 5 s pieces, so those are\nlong waits.\n\n**Want it fast?** Open `Freedom_Video_5B_fast.json` instead - the 5-billion\nmodel, ~1-3 min per clip, a bit softer motion.\n"
      ],
      "title": "READ ME FIRST  (14B model)",
      "color": "#322",
      "bgcolor": "#533"
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        780,
        -40
      ],
      "size": [
        420,
        120
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 51,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "14B is split in two. **1a** handles overall movement and layout, **1b**\nsharpens the fine detail. Both load; STEP 7 uses one then the other. You\nnever change these boxes."
      ],
      "title": "STEP 1 - the two experts",
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        780,
        -470
      ],
      "size": [
        430,
        400
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 55,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "These are two engines for turning a picture into a moving clip.\n\n**The big engine (this workflow)**\n- The movement looks real. Faces stay faces, hands stay hands, nothing\n  melts or wobbles between frames.\n- It listens. Type a detailed motion and it actually does that motion.\n- The add-on \"trick\" files - eyes rolling back, ecstasy face, finger\n  movement - are almost all built for this big engine. The small one\n  barely has any.\n- It works in two passes: first pass blocks out the big motion, second\n  pass cleans up the detail.\n\n**What the big engine costs you**\n- **Time:** ~8-15 min for a 5-second clip on this laptop. The small\n  engine does it in 1-3 min.\n- **Memory:** ~10.5 of your 12 GB of graphics memory, so the chat model\n  and other apps have to shut off while it runs.\n- **Disk:** two big files, ~13 GB together, plus a helper file. The small\n  engine is one 3.6 GB file.\n- Long clips (10 / 15 / 20 s) are made by gluing 5-second pieces\n  together, so they take a while.\n\n**Which one to use**\n- Just testing an idea, or checking a picture moves at all -> open the\n  file named `Freedom_Video_5B_fast`.\n- Something you want to keep, or using a trick file, or asking for tricky\n  movement -> stay here on the big one.\n- We picked a squeezed-down version of the big model on purpose, so it\n  just barely fits your graphics memory."
      ],
      "title": "WHY THE BIG MODEL (14B), NOT THE SMALL ONE (5B)",
      "color": "#2a2f3a",
      "bgcolor": "#3c4a63"
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1220,
        -40
      ],
      "size": [
        460,
        120
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 52,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "**STEP 4 (green)** fills from the queue slot - type in the queue panel,\nnot here. Write what MOVES. **STEP 5 (red)** is the \"no static\" list -\nleave it."
      ],
      "title": "STEP 4-5 - the words",
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        780,
        480
      ],
      "size": [
        420,
        320
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 53,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "A LoRA teaches ONE motion / expression. For 14B it must go on **BOTH**\nexperts - that's why there are two boxes (2a and 2b). Load the **same\nfile** in each.\n\n**Both are OFF now** (orange). To turn on: get a **Wan 2.2 / Wan 14B**\nLoRA (see `comfyui_ext/LORA_SOURCES.md`), drop it in the loras folder,\nright-click each box -> **Mode -> Always**, pick the file in both, and put\nits trigger word in your motion prompt.\n\n### strength_model  -  volume knob\n- **0.0** off  -  **~0.5** gentle hint (use if it distorts)  -\n  **1.0** normal, start here  -  **1.2-1.5** crank it (only if too weak).\nLeft = subtle, right = strong, too far right = broken. Keep 2a and 2b the\nsame number."
      ],
      "title": "STEP 2 - LoRA add-on  (both boxes)",
      "color": "#3a2a1a",
      "bgcolor": "#5a4020"
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1700,
        470
      ],
      "size": [
        620,
        240
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 54,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Two passes: **7a** (big-shapes expert) runs steps 0-10, **7b** (detail\nexpert) runs 10 to the end.\n\n- **cfg ~3.5** - Wan likes it low. Higher = stiffer, obeys words harder.\n- **steps 20** total is the norm. The split (10 / 10) is the two\n  start_at_step / end_at_step numbers - leave them matched.\n- **7a** seed control `randomize` = new motion each Run; `fixed` = keep\n  tweaking. **7b** stays `fixed`.\n- `return_with_leftover_noise`: **7a = enable, 7b = disable**. Don't swap\n  these."
      ],
      "title": "STEP 7 - two-stage sampling",
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        2340,
        740
      ],
      "size": [
        560,
        220
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 56,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Auto-saves to `output/freedom_video/`. **Set User Save Folder** +\n**Save to my folder** = your own copy (folder saved in the workflow).\n**Format**: MP4 default / WebM smaller / MOV for editors.\n\n**Extend video length** -> the clip goes back to the queue as a green\nslot (last frame + saved prompt). Run to add more onto the end.\n\n10 / 15 / 20 s presets auto-chain 5 s pieces - each piece is many minutes\non 14B."
      ],
      "title": "STEP 9 - save + longer",
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    }
  ],
